<!-- ── STRATEGY CARDS ── -->
<div class="strategies">
  <div class="strategy-card reveal">
    <div class="sc-num">Strategy 01</div>
    <div class="sc-name">Survival</div>
    <div class="sc-question">What do you do right now?</div>
    <p class="sc-desc">Immediate, short-term fixes for individuals or small groups. The underlying system doesn&rsquo;t change. The need is met today. Tomorrow the same problem returns.</p>
    <div class="sc-example">
      <span class="sc-example-label">Example</span>
      A neighbor drives one family to a clinic for medical care. The family&rsquo;s immediate need is met&mdash;but the clinic&rsquo;s restrictive hours and the transportation gaps remain for everyone else.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="strategy-card reveal">
    <div class="sc-num">Strategy 02</div>
    <div class="sc-name">Reform</div>
    <div class="sc-question">How do you improve the system you have?</div>
    <p class="sc-desc">Systemic improvements within the existing framework. More people benefit. The flow of assets improves. The community moves closer to the frontier.</p>
    <div class="sc-example">
      <span class="sc-example-label">Example</span>
      A community petitions the city for extended clinic hours and a new bus route. Access improves for a larger group. The flow of assets&mdash;doctors, medication&mdash;moves more freely within the current system.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="strategy-card reveal">
    <div class="sc-num">Strategy 03</div>
    <div class="sc-name">Agitation</div>
    <div class="sc-question">Who set the rules&mdash;and why?</div>
    <p class="sc-desc">Radical rethinking that challenges the design itself. Not improving the system&mdash;redesigning it. This pushes beyond the frontier. It redefines what &ldquo;optimal&rdquo; even means.</p>
    <div class="sc-example">
      <span class="sc-example-label">Example</span>
      Families campaign to overhaul healthcare policy altogether&mdash;ensuring that appointment times, locations, and funding structures reflect the needs of historically marginalized communities.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── CASE STUDY: NET GALA ── -->
<div class="case-break reveal">
  <div class="case-break-inner">
    <div class="case-break-label">Case Study<br>In Practice<br>LS&ndash;003</div>
    <div>
      <h2>From <em>House on Mango Street</em> to The Net Gala</h2>
      <div class="case-novel">Sandra Cisneros &mdash; Social isolation and identity formation</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="case-arc">
  <div class="arc-phase reveal">
    <div class="arc-phase-label">Movement 01<br>The Novel</div>
    <div class="arc-phase-content">
      <div class="arc-phase-title">Reading as Technology</div>
      <p class="arc-phase-text">Students read Sandra Cisneros&rsquo;s <em>House on Mango Street</em>, analyzing the consequences of social isolation on identity formation. The novel renders a system: what happens to a young person&rsquo;s sense of possibility when their world is small by design.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="arc-phase reveal">
    <div class="arc-phase-label">Movement 02<br>The Overlay</div>
    <div class="arc-phase-content">
      <div class="arc-phase-title">Data from Their Own Community</div>
      <p class="arc-phase-text">Literary analysis became the basis for research on their peers&rsquo; career aspirations versus representation. They discovered that a high percentage of their peers wanted to become healthcare professionals&mdash;but did not personally know a single healthcare professional.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="arc-phase reveal">
    <div class="arc-phase-label">Movement 03<br>The Hypothesis</div>
    <div class="arc-phase-content">
      <div class="arc-phase-title">The Gap Is Visibility</div>
      <p class="arc-phase-text">The system Cisneros rendered&mdash;isolation shaping aspiration&mdash;was operating in their own community. The asset existed (desire). The flow was blocked (no connection to the profession). The strategic response: create the connection.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="arc-phase reveal">
    <div class="arc-phase-label">Movement 04<br>The Intervention</div>
    <div class="arc-phase-content">
      <div class="arc-phase-title">The Net Gala</div>
      <p class="arc-phase-text">Using their literacy skills&mdash;proposal writing, data storytelling, strategic communication&mdash;students designed The Net Gala: a networking event modeled after the Met Gala that brought together 100 young people with 50 healthcare professionals. The Net Gala is now NewComm&rsquo;s official annual fundraiser.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="outcome-strip reveal">
  <div class="outcome-inner">
    <div class="outcome-label">The Arc</div>
    <p class="outcome-text">Critical reading of fiction led to data-driven community intervention, sustained by strategic writing and communication. A novel became an event. An event became an institution.</p>
  </div>
</div>

